 of the Rooster or Year of the Ox, things might get weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:50:31-08:00","id":1363472,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t their Were-Bulls in the past? Maybe they could do more symbolic things,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:53:29-08:00","id":1363473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363320-it\u2019s-the-eastern-year-of-the-rat-hooray-for-the-ratkin-and-bone-gnawers?p=1363464#post1363464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Now I keep thinking it would be kind of cool to have a set of &quot;Year of&quot; books for the Storytellers Vault. Like a Year of the Rat that looks at stuff like the Nezumi, the Asian Bone Gnawers, rat's spirit brood, ghoul rats for Vampire, as well as stuff about Nosferatu, maybe various Bygone and familiar rats for Mage, the idea of rat pooka for Changeling, and so forth. Year of the Dragon would be easy. I think when you get into Year of the Rooster or Year of the Ox, things might get weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Year of the Ox book, hypothetical material:<br /> - Mortals in vampire games (kine)<br /> - Apis, Apis, and more Apis!<br /> - Minotaurs as bygones, chimeras, and kiths<br /> - First book of material on oni, the second being the year of the Tiger.<br /> <br /> Year of the Rooster book, hypothetical material:<br /> - Shi(h) and Imbued, as the flashiest of vigilante forces guarding against monsters.<br /> - Corax, with deeply sarcastic and biting narration about lack of avian variety in the system. Mokole co-host some years, possibly adding in a fowl-related varna.<br /> - Technocratic Union<br /> - Doomslayers<br /> - Boggans<br /> <br /> I'm presuming that the Year of the Dragon involves yearly Mokole vs. Tzimisce grudge matches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T10:59:21-08:00","id":1363477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363320-it\u2019s-the-eastern-year-of-the-rat-hooray-for-the-ratkin-and-bone-gnawers?p=1363473#post1363473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Year of the Ox book, hypothetical material:<br /> - Mortals in vampire games (kine)<br /> - Apis, Apis, and more Apis!<br /> - Minotaurs as bygones, chimeras, and kiths<br /> - First book of material on oni, the second being the year of the Tiger.<br /> <br /> Year of the Rooster book, hypothetical material:<br /> - Shi(h) and Imbued, as the flashiest of vigilante forces guarding against monsters.<br /> - Corax, with deeply sarcastic and biting narration about lack of avian variety in the system. Mokole co-host some years, possibly adding in a fowl-related varna.<br /> - Technocratic Union<br /> - Doomslayers<br /> - Boggans<br /> <br /> I'm presuming that the Year of the Dragon involves yearly Mokole vs. Tzimisce grudge matches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait you could also do Satyrs in the year of the Ox cause in the WOD the Bulls were Gaia\u2019s matchmakers, and Goats are kind of like Bulls?<br /> <br /> Edit I just got why the Bogans are in the year of the Pig hard workers,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 01-26-2020, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T11:00:48-08:00","id":1363479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363320-it\u2019s-the-eastern-year-of-the-rat-hooray-for-the-ratkin-and-bone-gnawers?p=1363477#post1363477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait you could also do Satyrs in the year of the Ox cause in the WOD the Bulls were Gaia\u2019s matchmakers, and Goats are kind of like Bulls?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Satyrs would get both the Year of the Horse (originally, they had horse ears and tails) and the year of the Sheep/Goat (present appearances). The little cheats.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I guess trolls would probably be in the Year of the Rooster, wasn't thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-26-2020, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T11:19:14-08:00","id":1363484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363320-it\u2019s-the-eastern-year-of-the-rat-hooray-for-the-ratkin-and-bone-gnawers?p=1363419#post1363419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm's agents already hard at work in China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be Ratkin.<br /> Gaia knows the place is overpopulated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T11:51:21-08:00","id":1363486,"title":"","content":"China is really Wyrmy and Weavery , putting people in camps and being a Han supremacist state!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 01-26-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T18:59:49-08:00","id":1363550,"title":"","content":"Theoretical outline:<br /> <br /> Year of the Rat<ul><li>Stats for mundane rats, including as vermin swarms</li> <li>The Rat totem and her brood</li> <li>The various types of rats native to East Asia, including the giant rat of Sumatra (which is a real thing)</li> <li>The Wangtong Bone Gnawers of East Asia and the Beast Courts</li> <li>The Nezumi Ratkin of Japan and their counterparts in China and other parts of East Asia</li> <li>New gifts for Wangtong and Nezumi</li> <li>The legend of Raigo the Iron Rat</li> <li>Rat Yokai as Japanese Bygones, including fire-rats,</li> <li>Progenitor experiments in weaponizing rats</li> <li>A look at ghoul rats for Vampire</li> <li>An alternate Nosferatu centered form of Protean that involves transforming into a giant rat or into a swarm of rats</li> <li>The ghost rats which are briefly mentioned in the back of Orpheus</li> <li>The Great Hanoi Rat Massacre of 1902</li> </ul>Year of the Ox<ul><li>Stats for mundane oxen, cattle, water buffalo, and yaks</li> <li>Ox as a totem, as well as the Bull totem</li> <li>Ox-inspired Gifts</li> <li>Examining the Apis as they might have existed in prehistoric East Asia</li> <li>Ox-Head, one of the two demons who are fearsome guardians of the Yellow Springs</li> <li>The hero-king Chiyou and legendary emperor Shennong of China (possibly Apis)</li> <li>The Japanese god Tenjinsama</li> <li>The Japanese Kudan and other Bygones</li> <li>The Japanese ushi-onna as a possible Changeling kith</li> <li>Bull and Ox demons</li> <li>The Kindred habit of referring to mortals as Kine (cattle) and the Herd background</li> <li>Potence and Fortitude, and the concept of an Ox-inspired fighting style</li> </ul>Year of the Tiger<ul><li>Stats for mundane tigers, and a look at the various types of them in Asia.</li> <li>Tiger as a potential totem</li> <li>Tiger-inspired Gifts for Khan and others</li> <li>A look at the East Asian Khan of the Beast Courts, including the unique cultures of Khan in South East Asia and Indonesia</li> <li>The Tiger Army of the Wu Lung</li> <li>The White Tiger of the West</li> <li>A bit about the Howl of the Devil Tiger Dharma</li> <li>The tiger as an alternate Protean form</li> <li>The Tiger Style of Kung Fu</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-31-2020, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T17:29:06-08:00","id":1364071,"title":"","content":"Year of the Rabbit (and of the Cat)<br /> <br /> So, interestingly, the Asian Zodiac is not uniform throughout East Asia. While the Chinese version is the most well known, other countries have slight variations, and one of these is that Vietnam uses the Cat instead of the Rabbit. Which makes this next one a bit easier.<ul><li>Stats for rabbits and hares, as well as small cats</li> <li>Rabbit/Hare as a totem</li> <li>Potential rabbit (and cat) themed Gifts, Rotes, Talismans, Fetishes, and Treasures</li> <li>The legend of the Rabbit of the Moon, who in Chinese folklore is believed to be making the Elixir of Immortality, which ties in with the Wu T'ian.</li> <li>The story of the Hare of Inaba</li> <li>The Tokki as a possible new type of commoner Hsien</li> <li>The Bakeneko as a possible Japanese/Asian counterpart to the Bubasti and Cealican</li> <li>The Nekomata, the &quot;Cats&quot; described in the original A World of Darkness</li> <li>Cats (and rabbits) as familiars among East Asian Mages</li> <li>Cat and Rabbit Pooka in East Asian communities</li> <li>The Nyan type of commoner Hsien</li> <li>The mythical cabbit (a cat/rabbit hybrid) as a Bygone</li> </ul>Year of the Dragon<ul><li>Stats for crocodilians and other large reptiles of East Asia</li> <li>The importance of dragons in East Asian mythology, folklore and culture</li> <li>Crocodile as a totem from an East Asian/Beast Courts perspective</li> <li>Dragon themed Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans, and other artifacts</li> <li>The Zhong Lung Mokole, their place in the Beast Courts and how they vary around East Asia</li> <li>The Wyrm in East Asian/Beast Court cosmology and the Ebon Dragon</li> <li>The Azure Dragon of the East and a bit about the Black Turtle of the North</li> <li>A bit about The Thrashing Dragons Dharma</li> <li>A bit about the Wu Lung, the Dragon Emperor and the Dragon School</li> <li>Asian dragons as Bygones</li> <li>The Dragon King of the Sea</li> <li>Dragon Style Kung Fu</li> </ul>Year of the Snake<ul><li>Stats for various East Asian snakes, and snake venom as poison</li> <li>The place of snakes in East Asian cultures and mythologies</li> <li>Various serpent totems in the Beast Courts and East Asia</li> <li>Snake themed Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans, and other artifacts</li> <li>The Nagah among the Beast Courts and in East Asia</li> <li>The Fu Shi of the Hsien</li> <li>Empress Wa and the creation of mankind</li> <li>The Legend of Madam White Snake</li> <li>The nine-headed serpent monster Xiangliu</li> <li>The Japanese Buddhist goddess Benzaiten</li> <li>The Korean goddess Eopsin</li> <li>Snakes as familiars</li> <li>Serpent Bygones of East Asian, including the Bashi/Uwabami, Tsuchinoko, and Naga</li> <li>A look at the possibility of Setites in East Asia and their unique regional Cults</li> <li>Ghouled serpents</li> <li>Snake Pooka among East Asian communities</li> <li>Snake Style Kung Fu</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-31-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T18:30:57-08:00","id":1364079,"title":"","content":"&gt;Year of the Rat<br /> &gt; Viral pandemic break out in China<br /> Coincidence? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T19:25:21-08:00","id":1364264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1363320-it\u2019s-the-eastern-year-of-the-rat-hooray-for-the-ratkin-and-bone-gnawers?p=1364079#post1364079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Year of the Rat<br /> &gt; Viral pandemic break out in China<br /> Coincidence? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>While the outbreak has allegedly been traced to various Wuhan food venders selling wild animal meat (hedgehogs, baby crocodiles, bamboo rats, etc.) in both carcass and live form, if you wanted to build some sort of conspiracy story or doomsday plot out of it, Wuhan is also alleged to be the home of several of the Chinese regime's biowarfare labs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T19:42:32-08:00","id":1364266,"title":"","content":"Year of the Horse<ul><li>Stats for horses and equines in East Asia</li> <li>The place of horses in various East Asian cultures and mythologies</li> <li>Horse as a totem from a Beast Courts/East Asian perspective</li> <li>Horse related Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans, and other artifacts</li> <li>The White Horse in Buddhist culture and lore, including the White Horse Temple</li> <li>Horse-Face, one of the two demon guardians of the Yellow Springs</li> <li>The legendary horse Red Hare</li> <li>Shinto shinme horses</li> <li>The story of the golden horse from the Ainu of Hokkaido</li> <li>The War of the Heavenly Horses</li> <li>Horse-based Asian Bygones, including Longma (dragon horses), Tianma (heavenly horses), Boma, Chollima, and the Qilin</li> <li>Horses as familiars</li> <li>The ancient practice of horse burial and the potential of ghost horses in the Yellow Springs</li> <li>Horse-Hirayanu as a potential new type of Hsien</li> <li>Horse Pooka among East Asian communities</li> <li>The surviving Anda bloodline in modern day Mongolia</li> </ul>Year of the Goat (or Ram/Sheep)<br /> <br /> Another of those ones where the sign differs from culture to culture. The sheep/ram prevails in the north (Japan, Korea, Mongolia, and even some interpretations in northern China), while the goat does in the south (Vietnam, and some interpretations in southern China).<ul><li>Stats for goats and sheep (and other related bovidae)</li> <li>The role of goats and sheep in various East Asian cultures</li> <li>Totems such as Goat and Ram from the perspective of the Beast Courts and East Asian Garou</li> <li>Goat and Ram related Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans and other artifacts</li> <li>The Chinese goat god Yang Ching</li> <li>The ram's place in Asian shamanism and rituals</li> <li>The Japanese serow goat-antelope, one of Japan's national symbols</li> <li>The city of Ghuangzhou (Canton) and the Legend of the Five Goats</li> <li>Bygones such as the Xiezhi</li> <li>Goat and sheep as familiars</li> <li>Satyrs within East Asian communities</li> </ul>Year of the Monkey (because everything goes better with monkeys)<ul><li>Stats for various monkey (and possible ape) species of East Asia</li> <li>The role of monkeys in various East Asian cultures and folklores</li> <li>Monkey as a Totem from an Eastern/Beast Courts perspective</li> <li>Monkey related Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans, and other artifacts</li> <li>Sun Wukong, the legendary Monkey King, including his five methods of immortality and how they may apply to the Wu T'ian, Mages, Kuei Jin, and others</li> <li>Pha Treigen Changchup Sempa, legendary divine ancestor of the Tibetan people</li> <li>Sarutahiko Okami, Shinto lord of the crossroads between heaven and earth, and leader of earthly kami</li> <li>The Three Wise Monkeys (the &quot;See No Evil, Hear No Evil, Speak No Evil&quot; ones)</li> <li>The Hanuman of the Hsien (and perhaps why they are named after a Hindu character)</li> <li>The Yeren mockery breed, with a special focus on their infiltration of East Asian business and financial worlds</li> <li>The very mysterious were-orangs of Southeast Asia</li> <li>Monkey and ape Bygones, including natural Yeren, Vanara, the Bukit Timah Monkey Man, Mawas, the Yeti, the Hibagon, Orang Pendek, and Jueyuan</li> <li>Monkey familiars</li> <li>Monkey Pooka among East Asian communities</li> <li>Nanwan Monkey Island nature reserve in Hainan, China</li> <li>Monkey Style Kung Fu</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-02-2020, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T09:28:09-08:00","id":1364775,"title":"","content":"Year of the Rooster<br /> <br /> So, we have a lack of rooster and chicken related material for the WoD. However, certain Nepalese versions of the Zodiac just use Bird in place of Rooster, so I'm going to cheat by just talking about birds in general.<ul><li>Stats for various types of birds in East Asia</li> <li>The role of various types of birds in East Asian culture and folklore</li> <li>Various bird Totems, including Owl, Raven, Eagle, Rooster, Crane, Sparrow, and Magpie from the Beast Courts perspective</li> <li>Bird related Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans, and other artifacts</li> <li>A look at Falconry as a skill, and its place in the culture of Mongolia and other places</li> <li>The Tengu of the Beast Courts</li> <li>Were-chickens as a possible new mockery breed (ok, not really)</li> <li>The Fenghuang, the August Phoenix and its association with the Wyld</li> <li>The Crimson Phoenix of the South</li> <li>The Phoenix School of the Wu Lung</li> <li>Bird-type Bygones, including Qingniao, Luan, three-legged crows, Dapeng, Shangyang, Zhenniao, Kalavinka, and Inmyeonjo</li> <li>Birds as familiars</li> <li>The goddess Jingwei</li> <li>Karura as a possible new type of Hirayanu Hsien</li> <li>Bird Pooka among East Asian communities</li> <li>Crane and Eagle Styles of Kung Fu</li> </ul><br /> Year of the Dog<ul><li>Stats for various dog types in East Asia</li> <li>The place of dogs in East Asian cultures and folklore</li> <li>Why Dog isn't a Totem</li> <li>Dog oriented Rotes, Talismans and other artifacts</li> <li>The legend of Panhu</li> <li>The warrior god Erlang and his dog</li> <li>Dog Bygones, including Fu Dogs, the Tiangou, Penghou, and Raiju</li> <li>The Asian wild dhole, and it's potential as Garou kinfolk</li> <li>The raccoon dog and its place in Japanese folklore</li> <li>The Tanuki Hsien</li> <li>The Inugami as a potential new Hirayanu Hsien</li> <li>Dog Pooka among East Asian communities</li> </ul>I'm tempted to redo this as Year of the Canid and include a bunch of Garou and Kitsune stuff, among other things.<br /> <br /> Year of the Boar<ul><li>Stats for pigs/swine species of East Asia</li> <li>The role of swine in East Asian cultures and folklore</li> <li>Boar as a totem from the Beast Courts perspective</li> <li>Boar related Gifts, Rotes, Fetishes, Talismans and other artifacts</li> <li>The lost Grondr as the might've existed in East Asia</li> <li>Skull Pigs in East Asia</li> <li>Zhu Bajie, Pigsy of Journey to the West</li> <li>The Labours of Yamoto: The Demon Boar</li> <li>Swine Bygones, including the Babi Ngepet, the Bingfeng, Puaka,</li> <li>Pig-Hirayanu as a possible new type of Hsien</li> <li>Swine Pooka among East Asian communities</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-03-2020, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}